{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>We are all sons of one man, etc.</b> Meaning: and by this there is no room for suspicion of espionage, for spies would choose to be from many branches, and so you will find regarding the spies whom Moses sent (Numbers 13:2), and also the two whom Joshua sent (Joshua 2:1) — they were not sons of one man, for such is the way of one examining in this matter. And the verse's saying <b>we are upright</b> — meaning: after they make themselves known, it is justified that they are upright, for it is the opposite of the way of spies, who do not make themselves known of themselves." "<b>Your servants have never been, etc.</b> They spoke in the past tense — meaning, at their entry into the land. For now, after he had grown suspicious of them, they did not need to say that they were not spies, for surely they would not spy anymore. Or they may intend to say that after they stated their arguments to remove the suspicion of espionage from themselves, there is no basis to refute their arguments or to suspect them of being spies — unless they had already been spies previously, and therefore they said <b>your servants have never been spies</b> before, and therefore they would not now enter under suspicion."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:48:00.878432871Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}